# mkosi applies presets to the whole image, and Debian's presets enable anything
# not listed. Off: Debian's per-cluster WAL archiving and dump templates; backups
# are ours to schedule (D2), and an unconfigured pg_receivewal fails at every boot.
disable pg_*
# Debian's second caddy unit (config over its admin API). It binds the same ports
# as caddy.service, so whichever starts second fails.
disable caddy-api.service
# systemd-pcrlock writes its policy into /var, and cryptenroll then uses it by itself: a disk sealed
# that way needs that file to open the place the file is on. Found by test: the disk would not open.
disable systemd-pcrlock-*
# The screen is the app; a login prompt on tty1 is text flashing past at boot.
disable getty@.service
